SUMMARY:[Information Retrieval & Search][Recommender Systems] WWW 2027 - Fu
 ll-paper abstract deadline
DESCRIPTION:Conference title: ACM Web Conference (formerly International Wo
 rld Wide Web Conference)\nWebsite: https://www2027.thewebconf.org/\nSourc
 e URL: https://www2027.thewebconf.org/research-track-papers/\nLocation: D
 ublin\, Ireland\nTopics: Information Retrieval & Search\, Recommender Sys
 tems\, Graphs & Graph Learning\, LLM Agents & Tool Use\nSize: XL\nSubmiss
 ion type: Paper-based\nConfidence: confirmed\nLast checked date: 2026-10-
 30\nNotes: Full-paper abstract and paper deadlines (Oct 18/25 AoE) have p
 assed with no extension. The short-paper OpenReview portal was observed o
 pen on 2026-10-30\; separate mandatory abstract gates apply. Resource pap
 ers (four pages\, non-anonymous\, companion proceedings) are due Dec 17 A
 oE\; their portal is not public yet. OpenReview's short-paper forms close
  about an hour after the AoE cutoffs stored here. Demo papers (Nov 16 per
  the website)\, the PhD symposium (Jan 6 per the website) and the general
  workshop-paper date (Jan 4\, workshops not yet listed) are not tracked a
 s separate routes\; the OpenReview demo and PhD symposium forms are set t
 o close Nov 15\, 21:00 UTC. The Web4Good track is discontinued. Research 
 must substantively address the Web\, not merely use a web dataset. Preser
 ve WWW as the stable series alias. Size is an editorial estimate.\nScope:
  Research on the Web as infrastructure and a socio-technical ecosystem. C
 haracteristic ML-facing tracks include search and recommendation\, retrie
 val-augmented and agentic information access\, graph learning\, and seman
 tic knowledge. Responsible Web and privacy research are substantive stran
 ds. Merely using a web dataset or API is explicitly insufficient topical 
 relevance.\nAdditional topics: Knowledge Representation & Reasoning\, Dat
 a Mining & Data Science\, Fairness & Responsible AI\, Privacy-preserving 
 ML\, Ethics & Governance\nScope sources (2027): https://www2027.thewebcon
 f.org/research-track-papers/\nScope last checked: 2026-10-07
URL:https://www2027.thewebconf.org/research-track-papers/
END:VEVENT
